<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Entitlements for the hardened runtime, Developer ID distribution.

    Every entry below is load-bearing and is explained in CONTRIBUTING.md § 9. Two entries the
    Electron build carried are DELIBERATELY ABSENT:

      com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory
      com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit

    Both exist for V8, which JIT-compiles JavaScript at runtime. Swift is compiled ahead of
    time and needs neither. They are the two most security-relevant relaxations in the old
    set — together they permit writable-executable memory, which is the primary thing the
    hardened runtime exists to prevent — so dropping them is a real reduction in attack
    surface, not housekeeping. If a future dependency appears to need them, that is worth
    investigating rather than restoring.

    NOT sandboxed. The App Sandbox is incompatible with reading ~/Library/Messages/chat.db,
    which is the entire purpose of this application. Full Disk Access, granted by the user in
    System Settings, is what actually gates that read.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        REQUIRED for the Private API.

        The helper is injected into Messages.app with DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES. Library
        validation would refuse to load a library signed by a different team into a process,
        and this is the entitlement that stands down that check. Removing it does not produce
        an error message — dyld declines the insert and Messages starts normally without the
        helper, so the only symptom is a Private API that never connects.

        See .claude/docs/private-api.md and the arm64e note in docs/OBSERVATION_LADDER.md.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>

    <!--
        The AppleScript send path, which is the supported configuration for every user who
        has not disabled SIP. Without it, sends fail with a -1743 authorization error.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- Contact names and avatars on messages. The server runs without it, unnamed. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.addressbook</key>
    <true/>

    <!--
        Files the user chooses in an open panel — attachment sends, and importing a Firebase
        service account or a vCard.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
